> By the way, if you guys play rangers-- do you have a problem getting
> arrows, or do you just throw daggers?

	In the early game, I use any missile weapon I can get my hands
on. Daggers first, because they don't get permanently expended, then
arrows when I run out of daggers, darts as a last resort, and save any
enchanted arrows for emergencies.

	In the mid-to-late game, after the Quest, I #invoke up a few
hundred arrows, cancel them so they'll stack, then enchant them up to +7
or so, bless them, and poison them. And then don't use them most of the
time because by that point even a ranger can effortlessly melee his way
through pretty much anything in the dungeon, and without having to go
back and pick up after himself afterwards.

